Z||000003||Ken Wittlief||05-16-2001||04:45 PM||||most of the things you have listed as being replaced arnt the kinds of stuff you would normally take off a parts car, ball joints, tie rod end...<P>I usually keep my cars till the wheels fall off - its tough to decide when to let them go.<P>I dont know what your income bracket is, but if your taxes are up there, then donating the car to charity could be a $2000 charitable deduction off your itemized expenses - so if you are in the 30% bracket that comes out to $600 bucks off your next federal return payment.||||reg||1
